From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] [unit] Test how setupDataCall's arguments are written

Records the GBinderWriter calls the data driver makes for
setupDataCall_1_5 and setupDataCall_1_6, and checks that the 1.6
safe_unions OptionalSliceInfo and OptionalTrafficDescriptor go over as
buffer objects of their own, 24 and 56 bytes, all zero for noinit.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 unit/Makefile              |   1 +
 unit/unit_data/Makefile    |   7 +
 unit/unit_data/unit_data.c | 374 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 382 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 unit/unit_data/Makefile
 create mode 100644 unit/unit_data/unit_data.c

diff --git a/unit/Makefile b/unit/Makefile
index ce1c2cb..9d98b89 100644
--- a/unit/Makefile
+++ b/unit/Makefile
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@ all:
 %:
 	@$(MAKE) -C unit_base $*
 	@$(MAKE) -C unit_call_settings $*
+	@$(MAKE) -C unit_data $*
 	@$(MAKE) -C unit_devmon $*
 	@$(MAKE) -C unit_ext_call $*
 	@$(MAKE) -C unit_ext_ims $*
diff --git a/unit/unit_data/Makefile b/unit/unit_data/Makefile
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c8ed557
--- /dev/null
+++ b/unit/unit_data/Makefile
@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@
